-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
' INP applies the mask to the value read from the address. Two const masks
' are special: 0 leaves nothing of the value, and 177777 keeps all of it,
' so the compiler warns about both. A mask in a variable is not const and
' gives no warning.
10 A% = INP(1000, 255)
20 A% = INP(1000, 0)
30 A% = INP(1000, &HFFFF)
40 A% = INP(1000, 65535)
50 B% = 255
60 A% = INP(1000, B%)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
WARNING: at 6:9 line 20 - INP with mask 0 reduced to 0, consider to remove this INP.
WARNING: at 7:9 line 30 - INP with mask 177777 does the same as PEEK, consider to use PEEK.
WARNING: at 8:9 line 40 - INP with mask 177777 does the same as PEEK, consider to use PEEK.
